{"id":"torino-nice-rally","title":"Torino–Nice Rally","who":"Classic bikepacking route","when":"Mass start the first Friday of September; ride July–September","vehicle":"Gravel or mountain bike, 7–10 days","kind":"bike","color":"#dc2626","summary":"About 700 km and 15,500 m of climbing from Turin to Nice, half on high military gravel roads: the Colle delle Finestre, the Strada dell'Assietta ridge above 2,000 m, the Strada dei Cannoni, plus Izoard and Agnel. An unsupported group ride every September; the route is open all summer.","sources":[{"label":"Café du Cycliste: Tracing the Torino-Nice Rally","url":"https://www.cafeducycliste.com/en/blogs/rouler/tracing-the-torino-nice-rally"},{"label":"bikepacking.com: Torino-Nice 2024 (video)","url":"https://bikepacking.com/plog/torino-nice-rally-2024-josh-ibbett/"},{"label":"Rough Ride Guide: Torino to Nice","url":"https://www.roughrideguide.co.uk/route-details/2874"}],"approximate":"Main climbs named in reports; the rally line changes each year.","km":402,"bbox":[6.721,43.7005,7.6824,45.141],"stops":[{"name":"Turin","place":"Torino, Italy","at":[45.0678,7.6825],"text":"Start in the city.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Torino_Piazza_Castello_11.jpg/500px-Torino_Piazza_Castello_11.jpg","page":"Turin","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Torino_Piazza_Castello_11.jpg","credit":"Zairon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Colle delle Finestre","place":"Colle delle Finestre, Italy","at":[45.0717,7.0533],"text":"Giro climb, gravel at the top.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/ColleFinestre0001.jpg/500px-ColleFinestre0001.jpg","page":"Colle delle Finestre","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ColleFinestre0001.jpg","credit":"No machine-readable author provided. Idéfix~commonswiki assumed (based on copyright claims).","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Strada dell'Assietta","place":"Colle dell'Assietta, Italy","at":[45.0